    "readme": "Description\n===========\n\nMulti-subject, multi-modal (sMRI+fMRI+MEG+EEG) neuroimaging dataset on face processing. 16 young healthy volunteers were scanned once in MRI and once in MEG. During the task runs, the volunteers saw three types of faces (famous, unfamiliar and scrambled), either for the first time (Initial) or Repeated either immediately or after several intervening stimuli, but otherwise randomly intermixed every few seconds. This 3x3 design results in 9 different stimulus conditions: \n\n| Label                            | Simplified Label |\n|----------------------------------|-------"
